When the subscripted value is plausibly a 0-based .NET collection —
reached through a member, or last assigned from a member call or
LimsNetConnect — diag.zero_based_array_index drops to the info tier with
a message saying 0 may be valid there. A later reassignment from a
native value restores the error.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Bytes;
	:DECLARE oList, oNum, aBytes, vOut;
	oList := LimsNetConnect("mscorlib", "System.Collections.ArrayList");
	vOut := oList:Items[0];
	oNum := LimsNetConnect("System.Numerics", "System.Numerics.BigInteger");
	aBytes := oNum:ToByteArray();
	vOut := aBytes[0];
	aBytes := {1, 2};
	vOut := aBytes[0];
	:RETURN vOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Bytes;
	:DECLARE oList, oNum, aBytes, vOut;

	oList := LimsNETConnect("mscorlib", "System.Collections.ArrayList");
	vOut := oList:Items[0];
	oNum := LimsNETConnect("System.Numerics", "System.Numerics.BigInteger");
	aBytes := oNum:ToByteArray();
	vOut := aBytes[0];
	aBytes := {1, 2};
	vOut := aBytes[0];

	:RETURN vOut;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
9:17-9:18 error zero_based_array_index: SSL arrays are 1-based; index 0 is invalid. Use index 1 for the first element.
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:22-4:23 info zero_based_array_index: Index 0 on a .NET-derived value may be valid — .NET collections are 0-based. Native SSL arrays are 1-based; verify which one this is.
7:17-7:18 info zero_based_array_index: Index 0 on a .NET-derived value may be valid — .NET collections are 0-based. Native SSL arrays are 1-based; verify which one this is.
9:17-9:18 error zero_based_array_index: SSL arrays are 1-based; index 0 is invalid. Use index 1 for the first element.
